		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5045&amp;p=36661#p36661"><![CDATA[
Something similar happened to my RT3S once when I was using the factory firmware and contacted Retevis support and they gave me the following tip:<br><br>After the upgrades the firmware, turned off and turned on by pressing the two side buttons, so the machine will enter the lock frequency mode. please press the two side buttons again to boot it up.<br>It might be useful for you<dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="http://localhost/opengd77/download/file.php?id=2913&amp;sid=cc11c3beae49e9af0ee96b559da8938d" class="postimage" alt="rt3s botoes.jpg" onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2178">PU2RMT</a> — Tue Apr 08, 2025 3:51 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
